      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 18,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "text": "Venue, Event, Seat, and EventSeat describe what exists. SeatHold and Reservation describe actions over time. We update statuses instead of deleting history.\nEventSeat is the shared coordination point: competing transactions lock the same stable row before changing related lifecycle records.",
      "rawText": "Venue, Event, Seat, and EventSeat describe what exists. SeatHold and Reservation describe actions over time. We update statuses instead of deleting history.\nEventSeat is the shared coordination point: competing transactions lock the same stable row before changing related lifecycle records.",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Venue, Event, Seat, and EventSeat describe what exists. SeatHold and Reservation describe actions over time. We update statuses instead of deleting history.\nEventSeat is the shared coordination point: competing transactions lock the same stable row before changing related lifecycle records.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
